-- title:
--   The raw cyclic compiler agrees with the verified physical circuit
-- statement:
--   For every typed G₂ verifier V, erase its gate tags and finite wire indices to obtain its numerical raw circuit. Compiling that raw circuit produces exactly the erasure of the already verified coherent-certificate verifier:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{compileRaw}(\operatorname{erase}(V))
--    =\operatorname{erase}(\operatorname{compileVerifier}(V)).
--   $$
--
--   The equality includes proof and ancilla widths, the output wire, and the ordered gate list after conversion to standard verifier-wire order. It connects executable code generation to the physical completeness and soundness proofs.
